# Line endings are LF in the repository AND in the working tree, on every platform.
#
# Without this file, `core.autocrlf=true` — the Windows default, and what git for
# Windows sets during install — converts to CRLF on checkout. The result: a fresh
# clone on Windows fails `pnpm format:check` on 319 files before a single line has
# been edited, and `pnpm format` then rewrites all of them. Nothing in the repo
# explained why, because the machine this was built on had an LF working tree from
# before the setting was applied.
#
# `eol=lf` overrides autocrlf for checkout, so the trap cannot come back.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only tooling that genuinely wants CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Never touch these — git's own binary detection is good, but the screenshots are
# the README's shop window and a mangled PNG is a silent failure.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary

# Generated and vendored. Marking them keeps `git diff` and language stats honest.
pnpm-lock.yaml linguist-generated=true -diff
docs/permissions.md linguist-generated=true
